id: tool/stack
name: a Go program on the standard library alone, no third-party dependencies
prose: "The stack is the customer's demand, not the executor's choice: the tool is a Go program and it uses the standard library only. The module declares no requirements — go.mod carries the single module line and the go directive, nothing else; go list -m all names the main module and nothing but it; and the built binary's own build info contains no dependency line, so no third-party package rides inside the delivered program."
scope:
- go.mod
- build
- main.go
- picture.go
- entropy.go
- margin.go
covers:
- R1
rows:
- run: cat go.mod
  expect:
    rc: 0
    out: |
      module brim
      
      go 1.27
- run: go list -m all
  expect:
    rc: 0
    out: |
      brim
- run: test -z "$(go version -m ./brim | grep "^dep")" && echo "no third-party dependencies"
  expect:
    rc: 0
    out: |
      no third-party dependencies
